WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:01.968
-Thank you so much.
Enjoy yourself.

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.400
Thank you for being here.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.767
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:08.200
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:13.701
Well, guys, I saw that today is
National Singles Awareness Day.

00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:16.934
-Thank God.
[ Cheers ]

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:19.200
-Yeah, I could be wrong, but I'm
pretty sure that the day

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.033
when people are most aware
they're single

00:00:21.033 --> 00:00:22.300
is Valentine's Day,
but I don't know.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.567 --> 00:00:25.667
Actually, I think Singles
Awareness Day should be on

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:27.701
Thanksgiving 'cause that's when
your family makes you

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:28.934
the most aware you're single.

00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:30.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.701
"When are you going to date
somebody?

00:00:32.701 --> 00:00:34.300
"I want grandkids."

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:38.167
That's right.
It's Singles Awareness Day.

00:00:38.167 --> 00:00:40.767
And in a cruel twist of fate,
it falls on hump day.

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:44.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:47.367
Actually, single people are
like, "It's not that we don't

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:49.234
want to date someone, it's just
that we really enjoy

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:51.634
canceling plans."
I mean, that's fun.

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:53.734
That's right.
It is Singles Awareness Day,

00:00:53.734 --> 00:00:56.567
and this is nice -- stores
actually sold candy for it.

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:59.000
I think they might've just
reused some of

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.868
the candy from Valentine's Day.
Take a look. First there's...

00:01:04.601 --> 00:01:08.000
And you go, "Well, that's --"

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.200
Then there's...

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:14.334
And you go, "Wait, that's --"

00:01:14.334 --> 00:01:15.400
Next there's...

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:20.334
-Wow.
-That's more of a public
service.

00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:21.501
-For Smokey the Bear.

00:01:21.501 --> 00:01:22.834
-And finally, of course,
there's the classic...

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:27.734
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.367
"Not gonna happen."

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.901
Hey, in honor of Singles
Awareness Day, I just want to

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:37.667
take a moment to acknowledge all
the single people out there.

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:41.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:43.968
Don't worry if you haven't found
someone yet.

00:01:43.968 --> 00:01:46.133
Some people were single
throughout their 20s,

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:49.467
30s, and 40s.
And after a while...

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:51.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:56.067
...those people start to wonder
if "it" would ever happen.

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:58.701
And they practice kissing on
their pillows.

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:01.467
They even...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:05.367
They even post to Craigslist
seeking someone who likes to

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:07.834
"get freaky-deaky with a scalp
that's squeaky."

00:02:07.834 --> 00:02:12.734
[ Laughter ]
But in the end --

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:15.234
But in the end,
even that guy found love.

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:16.567
So keep the faith.

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:19.334
Worst case, you could just
accept a life of celibacy.

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:20.934
Hang in there, everybody.

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:23.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:25.067
Hey, James.

00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:31.300
That's what you get for not
coming to rehearsal.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.334
